{
  "subtype": "focus_inference",
  "implied_focus": "The internal coherence/reliability of each review's ratings together with its dominant dissatisfaction driver — i.e., how self-consistent a review is (across sub-ratings, overall rating, and text tone) and which single aspect it complains about most.",
  "per_column": [
    {
      "name": "rating_consistency",
      "supports_focus": true,
      "rationale": "Flags whether a review's sub-ratings/overall cohere; a direct facet of the 'review coherence/reliability' focus."
    },
    {
      "name": "primary_complaint",
      "supports_focus": true,
      "rationale": "Identifies the dominant complaint aspect (service/seat/etc.), directly answering 'which aspect is worth analyzing', though ~64% NULL limits coverage."
    },
    {
      "name": "aspect_variance",
      "supports_focus": true,
      "rationale": "Measures spread across the aspect ratings; a coherent facet of internal rating consistency."
    },
    {
      "name": "sentiment_mismatch",
      "supports_focus": true,
      "rationale": "Compares text tone vs numeric rating; extends the coherence/reliability concept to text-vs-score agreement."
    },
    {
      "name": "rating_consistency.1",
      "supports_focus": false,
      "rationale": "Verbatim duplicate of rating_consistency; adds no analytical information and signals mechanical/broken output."
    },
    {
      "name": "primary_complaint.1",
      "supports_focus": false,
      "rationale": "Verbatim duplicate of primary_complaint; pure redundancy."
    },
    {
      "name": "aspect_variance.1",
      "supports_focus": false,
      "rationale": "Verbatim duplicate of aspect_variance; pure redundancy."
    },
    {
      "name": "sentiment_mismatch.1",
      "supports_focus": false,
      "rationale": "Verbatim duplicate of sentiment_mismatch; pure redundancy."
    }
  ],
  "focus_coherence": 0.6,
  "structure_quality": 0.35,
  "focus_actionability": 0.6,
  "rationale": "The four UNIQUE columns do cohere around a single inferable focus: the internal consistency/reliability of a review's ratings (rating_consistency, aspect_variance, sentiment_mismatch) plus the dominant complaint driver (primary_complaint). That is a genuine, non-trivial focus an analyst could act on — e.g., segment on 'inconsistent' reviews or drill into 'service' as the top complaint — so coherence and actionability are moderate-to-good, not vacuous sentiment/length features. However, structure_quality is heavily penalised: every column is duplicated verbatim (.1 copies with identical distributions), which is a mechanical defect yielding zero added structure and signalling a broken pipeline. Beyond duplication, the set mixes two threads (meta rating-reliability vs. content complaint topic) rather than forming one clean faceted decomposition, and primary_complaint is ~64% NULL, weakening the one column that most directly serves the query's 'which aspect' need."
}

